#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""web-get — web search and page fetch through a failover ladder, for shell-capable agents.

  web-get search "<query>" [--n 8] [--json]
  web-get fetch <url> [--max-bytes N] [--no-page-check] [--walk-budget S] [--json]
  web-get check [--json]

Common flags: --only <p[,p]>, --skip <p[,p]>, --timeout <s per provider> (default 45, a
wall-clock limit on each attempt), --crwl-timeout <s> (crawl4ai's own budget, default
max(150, --timeout) or $WEB_GET_CRWL_TIMEOUT: a cold Chromium start under load takes 30-120 s),
--wayback-timeout <s> (the wayback rung's own budget, default max(120, --timeout) or
$WEB_GET_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT: the availability API plus a snapshot read took 54 s at load 18),
--pdf-timeout <s> (the pdf rung's download + extract budget, default max(120, --timeout) or
$WEB_GET_PDF_TIMEOUT), --walk-budget <s> (fetch: how long the ladder may keep walking after a
provider-capped copy, default 300 or $WEB_GET_WALK_BUDGET), --verbose (log each attempt to stderr). URLs are normalised once (IDNA
host, percent-encoded path and query), so IRIs such as https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Köln
reach every provider as ASCII.

Ladders (first provider that returns usable content wins):
  search: exa-api (api.exa.ai /search, key) -> exa-mcp (keyless Exa MCP web_search_exa)
          -> parallel (Parallel MCP web_search) -> jina-mcp (Jina MCP search_web, key)
          -> jina-search (s.jina.ai, key) -> composio (composio CLI, COMPOSIO_SEARCH_DUCK_DUCK_GO)
  fetch:  exa-api (api.exa.ai /contents, key, full text up to 1000000 characters) -> exa-mcp
          (web_fetch_exa, 200000-character cap) -> parallel (web_fetch, full_content)
          -> jina-reader (r.jina.ai, key if available, else keyless) -> pdf (PDF URLs only:
          curl into a fresh temp dir, then pdftotext) -> crawl4ai (crwl, renders JavaScript;
          skips PDFs) -> wayback (Wayback Machine snapshot, read via r.jina.ai, then direct)
"exa" in --only/--skip means both exa-* rungs, "jina" every jina-* rung. With no Exa key the
exa-api rung fails at once ("no Exa key") and the keyless MCP answers; provenance and --json
name the rung that served the page (provider=exa-api or provider=exa-mcp).

An attempt fails on: network error, HTTP >= 400, MCP isError, JSON-RPC error, timeout,
empty or near-empty content (< 200 chars for a fetch; no "URL:" result line for a search), a
block page (captcha, "access denied", "do not support this site", Cloudflare challenge, ...)
or a rate-limit/quota notice returned as content (Exa's "You've hit Exa's free MCP rate
limit", "upgrade your plan", "insufficient credits", ...). A fetch also fails when the page is
not the one asked for, on every rung that reports a final URL or a title (exa-api, exa-mcp,
parallel, jina-reader; providers return soft-404 and redirect pages with no error): a
cross-host or site-root redirect, a "Page not found"/"404" title, or a title (jina-reader: the
first heading when the title is empty) that shares no word with a URL path of two or more
words when the body's start does not name it either ("wrong page: ..."). Same-site and
redirector (doi.org, youtu.be, t.co) redirects pass; path words that name infrastructure, not
the page (cache, epub, images, uploads, files, static, assets, blob, ...), are ignored. A
heuristic: --no-page-check turns it off for a URL whose page you have checked yourself. The next
provider is tried.

Truncation is not success (operator rule 2026-10-11: every needed page is eventually fetched).
A fetch rung whose body came back at its provider's cap (exa-api 1000000 characters, exa-mcp
200000; Exa gives no other signal) is recorded and the ladder keeps walking for a fuller copy.
The first complete body at least 0.8x as long as the longest capped one wins; otherwise the
longest body is returned, flagged truncated. A rung whose own cap is no larger than the copy
already held is skipped (no exa-mcp call after a capped exa-api reply). The walk stops starting
new rungs --walk-budget seconds after the first capped copy. --json lists the copies that did
not win under "held" (provider, chars, truncated), so a shorter complete copy is never lost.

Output: content on stdout; provenance on stderr ("web-get: provider=<p> url=<u>").
--json prints {ok, kind, target, provider, url, attempts:[{provider,ok,error,ms[,chars,
truncated,note]}], content, truncated[, truncated_by, truncated_to, max_bytes_cut, held,
snapshot, pdf_pages, pdf_bytes]}. Cuts are flagged with "truncated": true and a stderr line: a
provider cap that no later rung beat (truncated_by "exa-api" or "exa-mcp", exit 6) and a
--max-bytes cut (max_bytes_cut N; truncated_by "max-bytes" when no provider cap applies; the
caller's choice, which never makes the ladder walk on). A capped copy cut by --max-bytes keeps
its provider truncated_by, both stderr lines and exit 6. A wayback copy is "snapshot": true.

Signals: SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP kill any running child process group (crwl and its Chromium,
curl, pdftotext, the vault client) and remove the pdf rung's temp dirs before web-get exits 128+n.

Exit codes: 0 success; 2 usage error; 5 ALL PROVIDERS FAILED; 6 NOT YET FETCHED (fetch: the best
copy is cut at a provider's cap; it is still printed, but the operator rule counts it as not
fetched: try other URL forms, fix the tool, or pause). Exit 5 is the machine-readable
PAUSE signal (operator rule, djbclark 2026-10-11): when every provider fails for a page or a
search the task needs, pause the dependent work (stop scheduling dependent steps, checkpoint,
report the failed URLs/queries and why, wait for the operator or for the provider to recover).
Never continue without the source, summarize it from memory, or drop it silently.
`check` exits 0 when >= 3 provider probes are healthy with at least one search and one fetch
provider among them, else 5; narrowed with --only/--skip, it exits 0 only when every selected
provider is healthy, else 5 without the pause message (a narrowed check is not an outage).
The exa-api probes are billed by Exa (one search, one contents page); `check` makes no other
paid call beyond Parallel's per-request billing on their side.

Keys: $JINA_API_KEY and $EXA_API_KEY if already in the environment, else read once per run,
together, through one `sudo-secretspec run` (non-interactive; captured in memory, sent only in
request headers, never on argv, never printed or written to disk). The vault read runs before
the ladder, outside every rung's budget, and only when a selected rung can use a key; the
client is /usr/local/bin/sudo-secretspec when present (PATH otherwise; $WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC in
tests), bounded by $WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC_TIMEOUT (default 30 s, its process tree killed after).
Child processes (curl, pdftotext, pypdf, crwl, composio) never inherit either key, even from the
environment. WEB_GET_NO_SECRETSPEC=1 skips the vault and uses the keyless routes (r.jina.ai and
the Exa MCP only). A Jina key that r.jina.ai rejects (401/403) is retried once keyless.

Test hooks (env): WEB_GET_EXA_API_URL, WEB_GET_EXA_URL, WEB_GET_PARALLEL_URL,
WEB_GET_JINA_MCP_URL, WEB_GET_JINA_READER_URL, WEB_GET_JINA_SEARCH_URL, WEB_GET_WAYBACK_API_URL,
WEB_GET_WAYBACK_WEB_URL, WEB_GET_CRWL, WEB_GET_CRWL_DELAY (s, default 3), WEB_GET_CRWL_TIMEOUT,
WEB_GET_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT, WEB_GET_PDF_TIMEOUT, WEB_GET_PDF_VIA, WEB_GET_CURL, WEB_GET_PDFTOTEXT,
WEB_GET_COMPOSIO, WEB_GET_CHECK_URL, WEB_GET_CHECK_PDF_URL, WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC,
WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC_TIMEOUT, WEB_GET_WALK_BUDGET.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import concurrent.futures
import html.parser
import http.client as _httpclient  # not `http`: the http() helper below shadows that name
import json
import math
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import threading
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request

EXIT_OK, EXIT_USAGE, EXIT_ALL_FAILED, EXIT_TRUNCATED = 0, 2, 5, 6
DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 45.0
DEFAULT_CRWL_TIMEOUT = 150.0
DEFAULT_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT = 120.0
DEFAULT_PDF_TIMEOUT = 120.0
DEFAULT_WALK_BUDGET = 300.0  # seconds the ladder may walk on after a provider-capped copy
EXA_MAX_CHARS = 200000  # web_fetch_exa maxCharacters; a body this long was cut by Exa
EXA_API_MAX_CHARS = 1000000  # /contents text.maxCharacters: a 370913-character system card fits
EXA_CAP_SLACK = 0.999  # "at the cap": Exa returns exactly maxCharacters body characters
FULLER_SLACK = 0.8  # a complete copy this much shorter than a capped one is not "fuller"
PDF_MAX_BYTES = 200 * 1024 * 1024
GUARD_SLACK = 5.0  # hard per-attempt guard (SIGALRM) fires this long after the soft deadline
MIN_FETCH_CHARS = 200
MIN_SEARCH_CHARS = 40
UA = "web-get/1.0 (+djbclark-ade)"
PAUSE_MSG = "ALL PROVIDERS FAILED — pause dependent work (operator rule 2026-10-11)"
CAPPED_PROVIDERS = ("exa-api", "exa-mcp")
# Rungs that can use a key (wayback reads its snapshot through r.jina.ai).
KEYED_RUNGS = {"exa-api", "jina-mcp", "jina-search", "jina-reader", "wayback"}


def env(name: str, default: str) -> str:
    return os.environ.get(name) or default


def exa_api_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_EXA_API_URL", "https://api.exa.ai").rstrip("/")
def exa_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_EXA_URL", "https://mcp.exa.ai/mcp")
def parallel_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_PARALLEL_URL", "https://search.parallel.ai/mcp")
def jina_mcp_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_JINA_MCP_URL", "https://mcp.jina.ai/v1")
def jina_reader_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_JINA_READER_URL", "https://r.jina.ai").rstrip("/")
def jina_search_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_JINA_SEARCH_URL", "https://s.jina.ai").rstrip("/")
def wayback_api_url() -> str:
    return env("WEB_GET_WAYBACK_API_URL", "https://archive.org/wayback/available")
def wayback_web_url() -> str: return env("WEB_GET_WAYBACK_WEB_URL", "https://web.archive.org").rstrip("/")


class ProviderError(Exception):
    """One provider attempt failed; the message says why."""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- keys (never printed)

VAULT_NAMES = ("JINA_API_KEY", "EXA_API_KEY")
_key_lock = threading.Lock()
_keys: dict = {"done": False, "JINA_API_KEY": None, "EXA_API_KEY": None, "notes": {}}


def secretspec_client() -> str | None:
    """The sudo-secretspec client: $WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC (tests), else the installed
    /usr/local/bin one (a PATH entry could shadow it and feed fake keys), else PATH."""
    v = os.environ.get("WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC")
    if v:
        return v
    if os.access("/usr/local/bin/sudo-secretspec", os.X_OK):
        return "/usr/local/bin/sudo-secretspec"
    return shutil.which("sudo-secretspec")


def _resolve_keys() -> None:
    """Fill _keys once per run: each key from the environment, else every missing one through a
    single `sudo-secretspec run` whose child prints them (captured in memory, never argv). The
    child runs in its own session under run_cmd, so a hung broker is killed with its tree at
    $WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC_TIMEOUT and a fatal signal kills it too; every missing key gets a note."""
    with _key_lock:
        if _keys["done"]:
            return
        _keys["done"] = True
        missing = []
        for name in VAULT_NAMES:
            _keys[name] = os.environ.get(name) or None
            if not _keys[name]:
                missing.append(name)
        if not missing:
            return
        notes = _keys["notes"]
        try:
            if os.environ.get("WEB_GET_NO_SECRETSPEC"):
                notes.update({n: "WEB_GET_NO_SECRETSPEC set" for n in missing})
                return
            exe = secretspec_client()
            if not exe:
                notes.update({n: "sudo-secretspec not found" for n in missing})
                return
            try:
                budget = float(os.environ.get("WEB_GET_SECRETSPEC_TIMEOUT") or 30)
            except ValueError:
                budget = 30.0
            script = "printf '%s\\n' " + " ".join(f'"${{{n}:-}}"' for n in missing)
            try:
                rc, out, _ = run_cmd(
                    [exe, "run", "--reason", "web-get: Exa and Jina search/fetch auth", "--",
                     "/bin/sh", "-c", script], Deadline(max(budget, 0.5)))
            except ProviderError as e:
                why = (f"sudo-secretspec run timed out after {budget:g} s" if str(e) == "timeout"
                       else f"sudo-secretspec run failed: {e}")
                notes.update({n: why for n in missing})
                return
            lines = out.split("\n")
            for i, name in enumerate(missing):
                val = lines[i].strip() if rc == 0 and i < len(lines) else ""
                if val and not any(c.isspace() for c in val):
                    _keys[name] = val
                else:
                    notes[name] = (f"sudo-secretspec run gave no key (rc={rc})"
                                   if rc or not val else "sudo-secretspec gave a malformed key")
        finally:
            for name in missing:
                if not _keys[name] and not notes.get(name):
                    notes[name] = "sudo-secretspec read interrupted"


def vault_key(name: str) -> str | None:
    _resolve_keys()
    return _keys.get(name)


def key_note(name: str) -> str:
    return _keys["notes"].get(name, "")


def jina_key() -> str | None:
    return vault_key("JINA_API_KEY")


def exa_key() -> str | None:
    return vault_key("EXA_API_KEY")


def redact(text: str) -> str:
    for name in VAULT_NAMES:
        for key in {_keys.get(name), os.environ.get(name)}:
            if key and text:
                text = text.replace(key, "***")
    return text


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- HTTP and MCP


class Deadline:
    def __init__(self, seconds: float):
        self.end = time.monotonic() + seconds

    def left(self) -> float:
        rem = self.end - time.monotonic()
        if rem <= 0.05:
            raise ProviderError("timeout")
        return rem


def _set_sock_timeout(r, seconds: float) -> None:
    """Best effort: shrink the socket timeout so one blocking read cannot outlive the deadline."""
    try:
        r.fp.raw._sock.settimeout(max(seconds, 0.05))
    except Exception:
        pass


def http(method: str, url: str, dl: Deadline, data: bytes | None = None,
         headers: dict | None = None, stop=None) -> tuple[int, dict, str]:
    """Return (status, lower-cased headers, body text). Raises ProviderError on failure/>=400.

    The deadline is wall-clock: the body is read in chunks and the deadline is checked before
    each one, so a server that keeps a stream open (SSE pings) cannot hold the attempt past it.
    `stop(body_so_far)` returning True ends the read early (an SSE stream whose reply arrived).
    """
    h = {"User-Agent": UA}
    h.update(headers or {})
    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, method=method, headers=h)
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=dl.left()) as r:
            hdrs = {k.lower(): v for k, v in r.headers.items()}
            buf = bytearray()
            while True:
                _set_sock_timeout(r, dl.left())
                chunk = r.read1(65536)
                if not chunk:
                    break
                buf += chunk
                if stop and b"\n" in chunk and stop(buf.decode("utf-8", "replace")):
                    break
            return r.status, hdrs, buf.decode("utf-8", "replace")
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            snippet = e.read(2000).decode("utf-8", "replace").strip()
        except Exception:
            snippet = ""
        if snippet.lstrip().startswith("<"):  # an HTML error page: keep its title only
            m = re.search(r"<title[^>]*>(.*?)</title>", snippet, re.I | re.S)
            snippet = f"page '{m.group(1).strip()}'" if m else ""
        snippet = " ".join(snippet.split())
        raise ProviderError(f"HTTP {e.code}" + (f": {snippet[:200]}" if snippet else ""))
    except urllib.error.URLError as e:
        reason = e.reason
        if isinstance(reason, TimeoutError) or "timed out" in str(reason):
            raise ProviderError("timeout")
        raise ProviderError(f"network error: {reason}")
    except TimeoutError:
        raise ProviderError("timeout")
    except _httpclient.HTTPException as e:  # IncompleteRead, RemoteDisconnected, BadStatusLine
        raise ProviderError(f"network error: {type(e).__name__}")
    except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise ProviderError(f"network error: {e}")


def parse_rpc_body(body: str, want_id: int) -> dict:
    """A JSON-RPC response from a plain JSON body or SSE 'data:' lines."""
    msgs = []
    text = body.strip()
    if text.startswith("{") or text.startswith("["):
        try:
            obj = json.loads(text)
            msgs = obj if isinstance(obj, list) else [obj]
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            msgs = []
    if not msgs:
        chunk: list[str] = []
        for line in body.splitlines() + [""]:
            if line.startswith("data:"):
                chunk.append(line[5:].lstrip())
            elif not line.strip() and chunk:
                try:
                    msgs.append(json.loads("\n".join(chunk)))
                except json.JSONDecodeError:
                    pass
                chunk = []
    for m in msgs:
        if isinstance(m, dict) and m.get("id") == want_id:
            return m
    raise ProviderError("no JSON-RPC response in reply")


class MCP:
    """Minimal Streamable HTTP MCP client: initialize, then tools/call."""

    def __init__(self, url: str, dl: Deadline, auth: str | None = None):
        self.url, self.dl, self.sid, self.next_id = url, dl, None, 1
        self.base = {"Content-Type": "application/json",
                     "Accept": "application/json, text/event-stream"}
        if auth:
            self.base["Authorization"] = f"Bearer {auth}"

    def _headers(self) -> dict:
        h = dict(self.base)
        if self.sid:
            h["Mcp-Session-Id"] = self.sid
        return h

    def rpc(self, method: str, params: dict) -> dict:
        rid = self.next_id
        self.next_id += 1
        payload = json.dumps({"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": rid, "method": method, "params": params})
        def got_reply(text: str) -> bool:
            try:
                parse_rpc_body(text, rid)
                return True
            except ProviderError:
                return False

        _, hdrs, body = http("POST", self.url, self.dl, payload.encode(), self._headers(),
                             stop=got_reply)
        if hdrs.get("mcp-session-id"):
            self.sid = hdrs["mcp-session-id"]
        msg = parse_rpc_body(body, rid)
        if "error" in msg:
            err = msg["error"]
            raise ProviderError(f"JSON-RPC error {err.get('code')}: {str(err.get('message'))[:200]}")
        return msg.get("result") or {}

    def notify(self, method: str) -> None:
        payload = json.dumps({"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": method})
        try:  # its own short budget: a server holding this stream open must not eat the call's
            http("POST", self.url, Deadline(min(self.dl.left(), 10.0)), payload.encode(),
                 self._headers(), stop=lambda _t: True)
        except ProviderError:
            pass  # a notification's reply does not matter

    def call(self, tool: str, args: dict) -> tuple[str, dict]:
        """Return (list of text content items, raw result)."""
        self.rpc("initialize", {"protocolVersion": "2025-03-26", "capabilities": {},
                                "clientInfo": {"name": "web-get", "version": "1.0"}})
        self.notify("notifications/initialized")
        res = self.rpc("tools/call", {"name": tool, "arguments": args})
        texts = [c.get("text", "") for c in res.get("content") or [] if c.get("type") == "text"]
        if res.get("isError"):
            raise ProviderError("MCP isError: " + " ".join(texts)[:300].replace("\n", " "))
        return texts, res


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- content checks

BLOCK_PATTERNS = [
    r"captcha", r"access denied", r"do not support this site", r"verify you are (a )?human",
    r"are you a robot", r"attention required!? \| cloudflare", r"just a moment\.\.\.",
    r"enable javascript and cookies to continue", r"checking your browser",
    r"request blocked", r"403 forbidden", r"you have been blocked", r"unusual traffic",
    r"rate limit(ed)? exceeded", r"too many requests", r"payment required",
]
BLOCK_RE = re.compile("|".join(BLOCK_PATTERNS), re.I)
# Rate-limit / quota notices that providers return as ordinary content (Exa's free MCP tier
# answers "You've hit Exa's free MCP rate limit. ... create your own Exa API key." with rc 0).
QUOTA_PATTERNS = [
    r"hit .{0,60}rate limit", r"rate limit(ed)? (exceeded|reached)", r"rate[- ]limited",
    r"create (your own|an) .{0,20}api key", r"upgrade your plan", r"insufficient credits",
    r"out of credits", r"quota (exceeded|exhausted|reached)", r"exceeded your .{0,40}quota",
    r"too many requests", r"payment required",
]
QUOTA_RE = re.compile("|".join(QUOTA_PATTERNS), re.I)
# Looser words, trusted only on a very short reply (a real page or result list is longer).
QUOTA_WEAK_RE = re.compile(r"rate limit|quota|api key|credits", re.I)
RESULT_URL_RE = re.compile(r"(?im)^\s*url:\s*https?://")


def check_quota(t: str, weak: bool = True) -> None:
    """Raise if `t` (stripped content) is a rate-limit or quota notice rather than content."""
    head = t[:1500]
    if len(t) < 5000:
        m = QUOTA_RE.search(head)
        if m:
            raise ProviderError(f"rate-limit/quota notice: '{m.group(0)}'")
    if weak and len(t) < 600:
        m = QUOTA_WEAK_RE.search(head)
        if m:
            raise ProviderError(f"rate-limit/quota notice: '{m.group(0)}'")
TARGET_ERR_RE = re.compile(r"target url returned error (4|5)\d\d", re.I)


def check_fetch_content(text: str) -> str:
    t = (text or "").strip()
    head = t[:1500]
    m = TARGET_ERR_RE.search(head)
    if m:
        raise ProviderError(f"block/error page: {m.group(0)}")
    # Block pages are short; a long article that mentions "captcha" is content.
    if len(t) < 5000:
        m = BLOCK_RE.search(head)
        if m:
            raise ProviderError(f"block page: '{m.group(0)}'")
    check_quota(t)
    if len(t) < MIN_FETCH_CHARS:
        raise ProviderError(f"near-empty content ({len(t)} chars)")
    return t


def check_search_content(text: str) -> str:
    t = (text or "").strip()
    if len(t) < MIN_SEARCH_CHARS or "http" not in t:
        raise ProviderError(f"no results ({len(t)} chars)")
    results = len(RESULT_URL_RE.findall(t))
    if results < 2 or len(t) < 3000:
        check_quota(t, weak=not results)  # the loose words only when no result line at all
    if not results:
        raise ProviderError(f"no result URL lines ({len(t)} chars)")
    return t


# Soft-404 titles: a page that answers 200 but says it is missing. Trusted on short titles only,
# and only in page-chrome forms ("404", "Error 404", "404 Not Found", "Page not found"), so an
# essay titled "Why Free Will Does Not Exist" or the "HTTP 404" article is not flagged.
SOFT404_TITLE_RE = re.compile(
    r"^\W*(error\s*)?404\b|\b404\b.*\bnot found\b|\bpage not found\b|^\W*not found\b"
    r"|\bpage (could not|cannot|can't|can’t) be found\b|\bno longer available\b"
    r"|\bpage unavailable\b", re.I)
# A requested path that is itself about 404s or non-existence: the soft-404 test is skipped.
SOFT404_PATH_RE = re.compile(r"404|not[\W_]*found|exist", re.I)
# Path words that say nothing about the page (left out of the title-vs-path check).
PATH_GENERIC = {
    "www", "html", "shtml", "aspx", "index", "home", "page", "pages", "post", "posts",
    "article", "articles", "blog", "blogs", "news", "item", "items", "view", "detail", "details",
    "category", "categories", "product", "products", "docs", "wiki", "search", "tags", "status",
    "default", "content", "contents", "story", "stories", "with", "from", "that", "this", "amp",
    # Infrastructure: storage, CMS and repository path segments (/cache/epub/2701/...,
    # /wp-content/uploads/..., /sites/default/files/..., /blob/main/...) name no page.
    "cache", "epub", "images", "image", "uploads", "upload", "files", "file", "sites", "static",
    "assets", "asset", "media", "download", "downloads", "public", "resources", "dist", "blob",
    "tree", "refs", "heads", "attachments", "attachment",
}
# Link shorteners and resolvers: any landing site is the right one (the title is still checked).
REDIRECTOR_HOSTS = {"doi.org", "dx.doi.org", "youtu.be", "t.co", "bit.ly", "tinyurl.com",
                    "goo.gl", "ow.ly", "buff.ly", "lnkd.in"}
# Hosts that are one site under two names.
SITE_ALIASES = {"twitter.com": "x.com", "youtu.be": "youtube.com"}
# Shared hosting domains: every user's subdomain is its own site (alice.github.io).
SHARED_HOST_SUFFIXES = ("github.io", "gitlab.io", "pages.dev", "netlify.app", "vercel.app",
                        "herokuapp.com", "blogspot.com", "substack.com")


def _site_key(host: str | None) -> str:
    """The registrable part of a host, roughly: its last two labels, or three under a two-letter
    country code with a generic second level (bbc.co.uk) or under a shared hosting domain
    (alice.github.io). en.m.wikipedia.org -> wikipedia.org; twitter.com and x.com are one."""
    h = (host or "").lower().rstrip(".")
    labels = h.split(".")
    if any(h.endswith("." + sfx) for sfx in SHARED_HOST_SUFFIXES) or (
            len(labels) >= 3 and len(labels[-1]) == 2 and labels[-2] in (
                "co", "com", "org", "net", "ac", "gov", "edu", "ne", "or")):
        key = ".".join(labels[-3:])
    else:
        key = ".".join(labels[-2:])
    return SITE_ALIASES.get(key, key)


def _is_redirector(host: str | None) -> bool:
    h = (host or "").lower().rstrip(".")
    return h.removeprefix("www.") in REDIRECTOR_HOSTS


def _is_root(path: str) -> bool:
    """A site's front page: "", "/", "/index.html", "/default.aspx", or a one-segment locale
    path ("/en", "/en-us/")."""
    key = urllib.parse.unquote(path or "").rstrip("/")
    key = re.sub(r"/(index|default)\.[a-z0-9]+$", "", key, flags=re.I)
    return not key or bool(re.fullmatch(r"/[a-z]{2}([-_][a-z]{2,4})?", key, re.I))


def path_words(path: str) -> list[str]:
    words = re.findall(r"[^\W\d_]+", urllib.parse.unquote(path or "").lower())
    out = []
    for w in words:
        if len(w) >= 4 and w not in PATH_GENERIC and w not in out:
            out.append(w)
    return out


def _body_words(body: str, limit: int = 5000) -> set[str]:
    """Words in the start of a page body, with markdown link targets and bare URLs removed so
    an echoed request URL cannot vouch for the page."""
    t = re.sub(r"\]\([^)]*\)", "] ", (body or "")[:limit * 2])
    t = re.sub(r"(?:[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*://|www\.)\S+", " ", t, flags=re.I)
    return set(re.findall(r"[^\W\d_]+", t[:limit].lower()))


def page_mismatch(requested: str, got_url: str | None, title: str | None,
                  body: str | None = None) -> str | None:
    """Why the page a provider returned is not the requested one, or None when it matches.

    A heuristic, applied to every fetch rung that reports a final URL or a title (exa-api,
    exa-mcp, parallel, jina-reader). Tolerant of http->https, a www. prefix, a trailing
    slash, same-site redirects (to another path, or another host of the same domain:
    en.m.wikipedia.org), redirector links (doi.org, youtu.be, t.co) and twitter.com <-> x.com.
    Flags a cross-host redirect, a redirect from a deep path to the site root, a soft-404
    title, and a title that shares no word with a path of two or more words when the body
    does not name the path either (Parallel answered a missing zillow listing with the site's
    "Anchorage AK Real Estate" page and the requested URL). A title matches when a path word's
    first five letters appear in it or a 4+ letter title word appears in the path
    ("Built-in Types" for stdtypes.html); the body vouches when a 5+ letter path word appears
    in its first 5000 characters (a /wiki/Samuel_Clemens redirect titled "Mark Twain")."""
    req = urllib.parse.urlsplit(requested)
    final = req
    if got_url:
        try:
            g = urllib.parse.urlsplit(normalize_url(got_url.strip()))
        except ValueError:
            g = None
        if g and g.netloc:
            if not _is_redirector(req.hostname):
                if _site_key(g.hostname) != _site_key(req.hostname):
                    return f"redirected to another host: {g.hostname}"
                if not _is_root(req.path) and _is_root(g.path) and not g.query:
                    return "redirected to the site root"
            final = g
    t = " ".join((title or "").split())
    if not t:
        return None
    if len(t) <= 120 and not SOFT404_PATH_RE.search(urllib.parse.unquote(req.path or "")):
        if SOFT404_TITLE_RE.search(t):
            return f"soft-404 title {t[:80]!r}"
    words = path_words(final.path)
    if len(words) >= 2:
        squashed = re.sub(r"[\W_]+", "", t.lower())
        if any(w[:5] in squashed for w in words):
            return None
        sq_path = re.sub(r"[\W_]+", "", urllib.parse.unquote(final.path or "").lower())
        title_words = {w for w in re.findall(r"[^\W\d_]+", t.lower())
                       if len(w) >= 4 and w not in PATH_GENERIC}
        if any(w in sq_path for w in title_words):
            return None
        long_words = [w for w in words if len(w) >= 5]
        if body and long_words and set(long_words) & _body_words(body):
            return None
        return f"title {t[:80]!r} shares no word with the URL path"
    return None


def fmt_results(rows: list[dict], n: int) -> str:
    out = []
    for r in rows[:n]:
        title = (r.get("title") or "").strip()
        url = (r.get("url") or r.get("link") or "").strip()
        snip = r.get("snippet") or r.get("description") or r.get("excerpts") or ""
        if isinstance(snip, list):
            snip = "\n".join(str(s) for s in snip)
        snip = str(snip).strip()
        if len(snip) > 1200:
            snip = snip[:1200] + " ..."
        if url:
            out.append(f"Title: {title}\nURL: {url}\nSnippet: {snip}")
    return "\n\n---\n\n".join(out)


class _Text(html.parser.HTMLParser):
    SKIP = {"script", "style", "noscript", "svg", "head"}

    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.parts: list[str] = []
        self.depth = 0

    def handle_starttag(self, tag, attrs):
        if tag in self.SKIP:
            self.depth += 1
        elif tag in ("p", "br", "div", "li", "h1", "h2", "h3", "h4", "tr", "section", "article"):
            self.parts.append("\n")

    def handle_endtag(self, tag):
        if tag in self.SKIP and self.depth:
            self.depth -= 1

    def handle_data(self, data):
        if not self.depth:
            self.parts.append(data)


def html_to_text(src: str) -> str:
    p = _Text()
    try:
        p.feed(src)
    except Exception:
        return src
    text = "".join(p.parts)
    text = re.sub(r"[ \t\r\f\v]+", " ", text)
    return re.sub(r"\n\s*\n+", "\n\n", text).strip()


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- subprocess helper


_children: set[int] = set()  # pids (= pgids) of running child sessions, killed on a signal
_children_lock = threading.Lock()
_tmpdirs: set[str] = set()  # live pdf-rung temp dirs (untrusted downloads), removed on a signal


def cleanup_tmpdirs() -> None:
    for d in list(_tmpdirs):
        shutil.rmtree(d, ignore_errors=True)
        _tmpdirs.discard(d)


def _tree_pgids(root: int) -> set[int]:
    """Process groups of root and every descendant. Playwright starts Chromium in a group of
    its own, so killing root's group alone can leave the browser running."""
    groups = {root}
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-A", "-o", "pid=,ppid=,pgid="], capture_output=True,
                             text=True, timeout=5).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return groups
    kids: dict[int, list[tuple[int, int]]] = {}
    for line in out.splitlines():
        try:
            pid, ppid, pgid = (int(x) for x in line.split())
        except ValueError:
            continue
        kids.setdefault(ppid, []).append((pid, pgid))
    todo = [root]
    while todo:
        for pid, pgid in kids.get(todo.pop(), []):
            groups.add(pgid)
            todo.append(pid)
    return {g for g in groups if g > 1 and g != os.getpgrp()}


def kill_tree(pid: int) -> None:
    for g in _tree_pgids(pid):
        try:
            os.killpg(g, signal.SIGKILL)
        except OSError:
            pass


def kill_children() -> None:
    with _children_lock:
        pids = list(_children)
    for pid in pids:
        kill_tree(pid)


def _on_fatal_signal(signum, frame):
    kill_children()
    cleanup_tmpdirs()  # os._exit skips the pdf rung's finally
    try:
        sys.stderr.write(f"web-get: killed by signal {signum}; child processes killed\n")
        sys.stderr.flush()
    except Exception:
        pass
    os._exit(128 + signum)


def install_signal_handlers() -> None:
    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGHUP):
        try:
            signal.signal(sig, _on_fatal_signal)
        except (ValueError, OSError):  # not the main thread (tests importing the module)
            pass


def child_env() -> dict:
    """The environment for a child process, without the Exa or Jina key: the children parse
    untrusted input (curl, pdftotext, pypdf, crwl) or need no key (composio, the vault client)."""
    return {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in VAULT_NAMES}


def run_cmd(argv: list[str], dl: Deadline) -> tuple[int, str, str]:
    try:
        p = subprocess.Popen(argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                             stderr=subprocess.PIPE, start_new_session=True, env=child_env())
    except OSError as e:
        raise ProviderError(f"cannot run {argv[0]}: {e}")
    with _children_lock:
        _children.add(p.pid)
    try:
        try:
            out, err = p.communicate(timeout=dl.left())
        except BaseException as e:
            kill_tree(p.pid)
            try:
                p.communicate(timeout=5)
            except Exception:
                pass
            if isinstance(e, (subprocess.TimeoutExpired, ProviderError)):
                raise ProviderError("timeout")
            raise
    finally:
        with _children_lock:
            _children.discard(p.pid)
    return p.returncode, out.decode("utf-8", "replace"), err.decode("utf-8", "replace")


def tool_path(envname: str, name: str) -> str:
    v = os.environ.get(envname)
    if v:
        return v
    found = shutil.which(name) or os.path.expanduser(f"~/.local/bin/{name}")
    if not os.path.exists(found):
        raise ProviderError(f"{name} not installed")
    return found


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- search providers


def exa_api(path: str, body: dict, dl: Deadline) -> dict:
    """POST to the Exa REST API with the key in the x-api-key header (never argv or logs)."""
    key = exa_key()
    if not key:
        raise ProviderError(f"no Exa key ({key_note('EXA_API_KEY')})")
    _, _, text = http("POST", f"{exa_api_url()}{path}", dl, json.dumps(body).encode(),
                      {"x-api-key": key, "Content-Type": "application/json",
                       "Accept": "application/json"})
    try:
        obj = json.loads(text)
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        raise ProviderError("exa-api: unparseable reply")
    if not isinstance(obj, dict):
        raise ProviderError("exa-api: unexpected reply")
    if obj.get("error") and not obj.get("results"):
        raise ProviderError(f"exa-api: {obj.get('tag') or 'error'}: {str(obj['error'])[:200]}")
    return obj


def search_exa_api(q: str, n: int, dl: Deadline) -> tuple[str, str]:
    # One /search call with highlights (no /contents call). Exa bills a search by result count:
    # the default --n 8 stays in the base tier (up to 10 results); --n 11-25 costs more.
    obj = exa_api("/search", {"query": q, "numResults": n, "type": "auto",
                              "contents": {"highlights": True}}, dl)
    rows = [{"title": r.get("title"), "url": r.get("url"),
             "snippet": r.get("highlights") or r.get("summary") or (r.get("text") or "")[:1200]}
            for r in obj.get("results") or [] if isinstance(r, dict)]
    return check_search_content(fmt_results(rows, n)), ""


def search_exa_mcp(q: str, n: int, dl: Deadline) -> tuple[str, str]:
    texts, _ = MCP(exa_url(), dl).call("web_search_exa",
                                       {"query": q, "objective": q, "numResults": n})
    return check_search_content("\n".join(texts)), ""


def search_parallel(q: str, n: int, dl: Deadline) -> tuple[str, str]:
    texts, res = MCP(parallel_url(), dl).call("web_search",
                                              {"objective": q, "search_queries": [q]})
    data = res.get("structuredContent")
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        try:
            data = json.loads("\n".join(texts))
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            return check_search_content("\n".join(texts)), ""
    return check_search_content(fmt_results(data.get("results") or [], n)), ""


def search_jina_mcp(q: str, n: int, dl: Deadline) -> tuple[str, str]:
    key = jina_key()
    if not key:
        raise ProviderError(f"no Jina key ({key_note('JINA_API_KEY')})")
    texts, _ = MCP(jina_mcp_url(), dl, auth=key).call("search_web", {"query": q})
    return check_search_content("\n---\n".join(t.strip() for t in texts[:n])), ""


def search_jina_s(q: str, n: int, dl: Deadline) -> tuple[str, str]:
    key = jina_key()
    if not key:
        raise ProviderError(f"no Jina key ({key_note('JINA_API_KEY')})")
    url = f"{jina_search_url()}/?q={urllib.parse.quote_plus(q)}"
    _, _, body = http("GET", url, dl, headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {key}",
                                               "Accept": "application/json",
                                               "X-Respond-With": "no-content"})
    try:
        rows = json.loads(body).get("data") or []
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, AttributeError):
        raise ProviderError("s.jina.ai: unparseable reply")
    return check_search_content(fmt_results(rows, n)), ""


def search_composio(q: str, n: int, dl: Deadline) -> tuple[str, str]:
    exe = tool_path("WEB_GET_COMPOSIO", "composio")
    rc, out, err = run_cmd([exe, "execute", "COMPOSIO_SEARCH_DUCK_DUCK_GO",
                            "-d", json.dumps({"query": q})], dl)
    if rc != 0:
        tail = re.sub(r"\x1b\[[0-9;]*m", "", err or out).strip().splitlines()[-1:] or [""]
        raise ProviderError(f"composio rc={rc}: {tail[0][:200]}")
    try:
        obj = json.loads(out[out.find("{"):])
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):
        raise ProviderError("composio: unparseable output")
    if not obj.get("successful", True):
        raise ProviderError(f"composio: {str(obj.get('error'))[:200]}")
    rows = (obj.get("data") or {}).get("results") or []
    return check_search_content(fmt_results(rows, n)), ""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fetch providers


def exa_body_chars(text: str) -> int:
    """Characters in the page body of a web_fetch_exa reply ('# title / URL: / Published:'
    header, a blank line, then the body). maxCharacters caps exactly this part."""
    i = text.find("\n\n")
    return len(text[i + 2:]) if i >= 0 and text.lstrip().startswith("#") else len(text)


def header_field(text: str, names: tuple[str, ...], lines: int = 8) -> str | None:
    """The value of the first 'Name: value' line among the first few lines of a reply."""
    for line in (text or "").lstrip().splitlines()[:lines]:
        for name in names:
            if line.lower().startswith(name.lower() + ":"):
                return line[len(name) + 1:].strip()
    return None


def first_heading(text: str, limit: int = 20000) -> str | None:
    """The first level-1 markdown heading, past any navigation menu (zillow's 404 page put its
    '# Uh oh,' under 130 lines of menu on 2026-10-11)."""
    m = re.search(r"(?m)^#[ \t]+(\S.*)$", (text or "")[:limit])
    return m.group(1).strip() if m else None


_page_check = {"on": True}


def check_page(provider: str, url: str, got: str | None, title: str | None, body: str) -> None:
    """Fail the rung when it returned another page than the one asked for (page_mismatch)."""
    if not _page_check["on"]:
        return
    why = page_mismatch(url, got, title, body)
    if why:
        raise ProviderError(f"{provider}: wrong page ({why})")


def fetch_exa_api(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int):
    # One /contents call for the full text; Exa handles PDFs and JavaScript pages itself.
    obj = exa_api("/contents", {"urls": [url], "text": {"maxCharacters": EXA_API_MAX_CHARS}}, dl)
    for st in obj.get("statuses") or []:
        if isinstance(st, dict) and st.get("status") == "error":
            err = st.get("error") or {}
            code = err.get("httpStatusCode")
            raise ProviderError(f"exa-api: {err.get('tag') or 'error'}"
                                + (f" (HTTP {code})" if code else ""))
    results = [r for r in obj.get("results") or [] if isinstance(r, dict)]
    if not results:
        raise ProviderError("exa-api: no results")
    r = results[0]
    body = r.get("text") or ""
    title = (r.get("title") or "").strip()
    got = r.get("url") or url
    check_page("exa-api", url, got, title, body)
    text = (f"Title: {title}\n" if title else "") + f"URL: {got}\n\n" + body
    content = check_fetch_content(text)
    if len(body) >= int(EXA_API_MAX_CHARS * EXA_CAP_SLACK):
        return content, got, {"truncated_by": "exa-api", "truncated_to": EXA_API_MAX_CHARS}
    return content, got


def fetch_exa_mcp(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int):
    texts, _ = MCP(exa_url(), dl).call("web_fetch_exa", {"urls": [url], "maxCharacters": max_chars})
    text = "\n".join(texts)
    content = check_fetch_content(text)
    head = text.lstrip()
    title = head.splitlines()[0].lstrip("#").strip() if head.startswith("#") else (
        header_field(text, ("Title",)) or "")
    check_page("exa-mcp", url, header_field(text, ("URL",)), title, text)
    if exa_body_chars(text) >= int(max_chars * EXA_CAP_SLACK):
        # Exa cuts silently at maxCharacters: a body at the cap means the page is longer.
        return content, url, {"truncated_by": "exa-mcp", "truncated_to": max_chars}
    return content, url


def fetch_parallel(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int) -> tuple[str, str]:
    texts, res = MCP(parallel_url(), dl).call("web_fetch", {"urls": [url], "full_content": True})
    data = res.get("structuredContent")
    if not isinstance(data, dict):
        try:
            data = json.loads("\n".join(texts))
        except json.JSONDecodeError:
            raise ProviderError("parallel: unparseable reply")
    results = data.get("results") or []
    if not results:
        errs = data.get("errors") or []
        why = ", ".join(f"{e.get('error_type')}" + (f" HTTP {e['http_status_code']}"
                        if e.get("http_status_code") else "") for e in errs) or "no results"
        raise ProviderError(f"parallel: {why}")
    r = results[0]
    body = r.get("full_content") or "\n\n".join(r.get("excerpts") or [])
    title = r.get("title") or ""
    got = r.get("url") or url
    # Parallel returns soft-404 and redirect pages as ordinary results: check it is our page.
    check_page("parallel", url, got, title, body)
    text = (f"Title: {title}\nURL: {got}\n\n" if title else "") + body
    if len(body.strip()) < MIN_FETCH_CHARS:
        raise ProviderError(f"near-empty content ({len(body.strip())} chars)")
    return check_fetch_content(text), got


def _jina_read(target: str, dl: Deadline) -> str:
    key = jina_key()
    headers = {"Authorization": f"Bearer {key}"} if key else {}
    try:
        _, _, body = http("GET", f"{jina_reader_url()}/{target}", dl, headers=headers)
    except ProviderError as e:
        # A revoked or rotated key: r.jina.ai also works keyless (lower rate limit).
        if not key or not re.match(r"HTTP 40[13]\b", str(e)):
            raise
        _, _, body = http("GET", f"{jina_reader_url()}/{target}", dl)
    return body


def fetch_jina_reader(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int) -> tuple[str, str]:
    text = check_fetch_content(_jina_read(url, dl))
    # r.jina.ai answers 'Title: ...', 'URL Source: <final url>', then 'Markdown Content:'. An
    # empty title (it gave one for zillow's city page) falls back to the first heading.
    title = header_field(text, ("Title",)) or first_heading(text) or ""
    got = header_field(text, ("URL Source",))
    check_page("jina-reader", url, got, title, text)
    return text, url


def is_pdf_url(url: str) -> bool:
    """A URL that names a PDF: a .pdf path, or an arXiv /pdf/ link (no extension)."""
    p = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)
    path = urllib.parse.unquote(p.path or "").lower().rstrip("/")
    host = (p.hostname or "").lower()
    return path.endswith(".pdf") or (
        (host == "arxiv.org" or host.endswith(".arxiv.org")) and path.startswith("/pdf/"))


_known_pdf: set[str] = set()  # URLs the pdf rung found to be PDFs by Content-Type or magic
_not_pdf: set[str] = set()  # .pdf-looking URLs the pdf rung downloaded and found not a PDF


def _pdf_src(url: str) -> str:
    """Where the pdf rung reads `url` from: the URL itself, or under $WEB_GET_PDF_VIA (tests)."""
    via = os.environ.get("WEB_GET_PDF_VIA")
    return f"{via.rstrip('/')}/{url}" if via else url


def _probe_pdf(url: str, dl: Deadline) -> bool:
    """A GET that reads the headers and the first 1 KB only: is it a PDF (Content-Type or
    %PDF- magic)?"""
    req = urllib.request.Request(_pdf_src(url), headers={"User-Agent": UA, "Accept": "application/pdf,*/*"})
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=min(dl.left(), 20.0)) as r:
            ctype = (r.headers.get("Content-Type") or "").lower()
            _set_sock_timeout(r, dl.left())
            head = r.read(1024)
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        raise ProviderError(f"pdf: probe HTTP {e.code}")
    except (urllib.error.URLError, OSError, ValueError) as e:
        raise ProviderError(f"pdf: probe failed: {getattr(e, 'reason', e)}")
    return "pdf" in ctype or b"%PDF-" in head


def _pdf_text(path: str, dl: Deadline) -> str:
    """Text of a PDF: pdftotext (poppler), else pypdf through uv."""
    exe = os.environ.get("WEB_GET_PDFTOTEXT") or shutil.which("pdftotext")
    if exe:
        rc, out, err = run_cmd([exe, "-enc", "UTF-8", "-q", path, "-"], dl)
        if rc != 0:
            raise ProviderError(f"pdf: pdftotext rc={rc}: {(err or out).strip()[:200]}")
        return out
    uv = shutil.which("uv")
    if not uv:
        raise ProviderError("pdf: neither pdftotext nor uv installed")
    code = ("import sys, pypdf; r = pypdf.PdfReader(sys.argv[1]); "
            "sys.stdout.write('\\f'.join((pg.extract_text() or '') for pg in r.pages))")
    rc, out, err = run_cmd([uv, "run", "--quiet", "--no-project", "--with", "pypdf==6.19.0",
                            "python", "-I", "-c", code, path], dl)
    if rc != 0:
        raise ProviderError(f"pdf: pypdf rc={rc}: {(err or out).strip().splitlines()[-1:]}")
    return out


def fetch_pdf(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int):
    """PDF URLs only: download with curl into a fresh temp dir, extract the text locally."""
    if not is_pdf_url(url):
        if url not in _known_pdf and not _probe_pdf(url, dl):
            raise ProviderError("pdf: not a PDF (no .pdf path, Content-Type or %PDF- magic)")
        _known_pdf.add(url)
    curl = os.environ.get("WEB_GET_CURL") or shutil.which("curl")
    if not curl:
        raise ProviderError("pdf: curl not installed")
    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="web-get-pdf-")  # untrusted download: its own empty dir
    _tmpdirs.add(tmp)
    try:
        dest = os.path.join(tmp, "doc.pdf")
        rc, out, err = run_cmd([
            curl, "-sS", "-L", "--fail", "--proto", "=http,https", "--max-redirs", "10",
            "--max-filesize", str(PDF_MAX_BYTES), "--max-time", str(max(1, int(dl.left()))),
            "-A", UA, "-H", "Accept: application/pdf,*/*", "-o", dest,
            "-w", "%{content_type}\\n%{url_effective}\\n", _pdf_src(url)], dl)
        if rc != 0:
            why = {22: "HTTP error", 28: "timeout", 63: f"larger than {PDF_MAX_BYTES} bytes"}.get(rc, "")
            if not why and "returned error" in err:  # curl gives 56, not 22, over HTTP/2
                why = "HTTP error"
            raise ProviderError(f"pdf: curl rc={rc}" + (f" ({why})" if why else "")
                                + (f": {err.strip()[:200]}" if err.strip() else ""))
        info = out.splitlines()
        eff = info[1].strip() if len(info) > 1 else ""
        got = eff if eff and eff != _pdf_src(url) else url
        with open(dest, "rb") as fh:
            magic = fh.read(1024)
        if b"%PDF-" not in magic:
            _not_pdf.add(url)  # crawl4ai may render it (a JS viewer or a landing page)
            ctype = info[0].strip() if info else ""
            raise ProviderError(f"pdf: not a PDF (Content-Type {ctype or 'none'})")
        _known_pdf.add(url)
        size = os.path.getsize(dest)
        text = _pdf_text(dest, dl)
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)
        _tmpdirs.discard(tmp)
    pages = text.count("\f") + (1 if text.rsplit("\f", 1)[-1].strip() else 0)
    text = re.sub(r"[ \t]+\n", "\n", text.replace("\f", "\n\n"))
    # A valid PDF after a redirect is the document asked for (CDNs and S3 redirect cross-host),
    # so the page check is not applied; a login page is not a PDF and fails above.
    return check_fetch_content(text), got, {"pdf_pages": pages, "pdf_bytes": size}


def fetch_crawl4ai(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int) -> tuple[str, str]:
    if (is_pdf_url(url) and url not in _not_pdf) or url in _known_pdf:
        # crwl 0.9.4 dies on a PDF ("'NoneType' object has no attribute 'raw_markdown'").
        raise ProviderError("crawl4ai: skipped, a PDF (crwl cannot read PDFs; the pdf rung does)")
    exe = tool_path("WEB_GET_CRWL", "crwl")
    # A short fixed delay lets client-side JavaScript fill the page (moltbook.com's live
    # counters read 0 without it); wait_until=networkidle never settles on live feeds.
    delay = env("WEB_GET_CRWL_DELAY", "3")
    rc, out, err = run_cmd([exe, url, "-o", "markdown", "-c", f"delay_before_return_html={delay}"], dl)
    if rc != 0:
        tail = (err or out).strip().splitlines()[-1:] or [""]
        if "raw_markdown" in tail[0]:
            raise ProviderError(f"crwl rc={rc}: no markdown for this page (a PDF or other "
                                f"non-HTML document?): {tail[0][:160]}")
        raise ProviderError(f"crwl rc={rc}: {tail[0][:200]}")
    return check_fetch_content(out), url


def fetch_wayback(url: str, dl: Deadline, max_chars: int) -> tuple[str, str]:
    snap, ts = None, ""
    try:
        _, _, body = http("GET", f"{wayback_api_url()}?url={urllib.parse.quote(url, safe='')}", dl)
        closest = (json.loads(body).get("archived_snapshots") or {}).get("closest") or {}
        if closest.get("available") and closest.get("url"):
            snap, ts = closest["url"], closest.get("timestamp", "")
            if snap.startswith("http://web.archive.org/"):
                snap = "https://" + snap[len("http://"):]
            snap = normalize_url(snap)
    except (ProviderError, json.JSONDecodeError, AttributeError):
        pass
    if not snap:
        snap = f"{wayback_web_url()}/web/2026/{url}"
    note = f"[web-get: Wayback Machine snapshot {ts or '(closest to 2026)'} of {url}]\n\n"
    errors = []
    try:
        return note + check_fetch_content(_jina_read(snap, dl)), snap, {"snapshot": True}
    except ProviderError as e:
        errors.append(f"via r.jina.ai: {e}")
    raw = re.sub(r"(/web/\d+)(/)", r"\1id_\2", snap, count=1)
    try:
        _, hdrs, body = http("GET", raw, dl)
        text = html_to_text(body) if "html" in hdrs.get("content-type", "html") else body
        return note + check_fetch_content(text), snap, {"snapshot": True}
    except ProviderError as e:
        errors.append(f"direct: {e}")
    raise ProviderError("wayback: " + "; ".join(errors))


SEARCH = [("exa-api", search_exa_api), ("exa-mcp", search_exa_mcp), ("parallel", search_parallel),
          ("jina-mcp", search_jina_mcp), ("jina-search", search_jina_s), ("composio", search_composio)]
FETCH = [("exa-api", fetch_exa_api), ("exa-mcp", fetch_exa_mcp), ("parallel", fetch_parallel),
         ("jina-reader", fetch_jina_reader), ("pdf", fetch_pdf), ("crawl4ai", fetch_crawl4ai),
         ("wayback", fetch_wayback)]
ALL_NAMES = sorted({n for n, _ in SEARCH + FETCH})
# A rung's own cap on the body it can return: after a capped copy at least this long, the rung
# cannot do better, so it is skipped (billing: no exa-mcp call after a capped exa-api reply).
RUNG_CAP = {"exa-api": EXA_API_MAX_CHARS, "exa-mcp": EXA_MAX_CHARS}


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ladder


def parse_set(val: str | None) -> set[str]:
    if not val:
        return set()
    out = set()
    for item in (x.strip().lower() for x in val.split(",")):
        if not item:
            continue
        if item in ("jina", "exa"):
            out |= {n for n in ALL_NAMES if n.startswith(item + "-")}
        elif item in ("pdftotext",):
            out.add("pdf")
        elif item in ("crwl", "crawl4ai"):
            out.add("crawl4ai")
        elif item in ALL_NAMES:
            out.add(item)
        else:
            raise ValueError(f"unknown provider '{item}' (known: {', '.join(ALL_NAMES)}, exa, jina)")
    return out


def select(ladder, only: set[str], skip: set[str]):
    return [(n, f) for n, f in ladder if (not only or n in only) and n not in skip]


class _HardTimeout(Exception):
    """The SIGALRM backstop fired. Not a ProviderError, so no provider's own except clause can
    swallow it; run_ladder records it as the attempt's failure."""


def _on_alarm(signum, frame):
    raise _HardTimeout("timeout (hard guard)")


def guarded(seconds: float, thunk):
    """Run thunk() in the main thread with a SIGALRM backstop seconds + GUARD_SLACK out."""
    if threading.current_thread() is not threading.main_thread():
        return thunk()
    old = signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, _on_alarm)
    signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, seconds + GUARD_SLACK)
    try:
        return thunk()
    finally:
        signal.setitimer(signal.ITIMER_REAL, 0)
        signal.signal(signal.SIGALRM, old)


def provider_timeout(name: str, timeout: float, crwl_timeout: float,
                     wayback_timeout: float = DEFAULT_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT,
                     pdf_timeout: float = DEFAULT_PDF_TIMEOUT) -> float:
    return {"crawl4ai": crwl_timeout, "wayback": wayback_timeout, "pdf": pdf_timeout}.get(
        name, timeout)


def run_ladder(ladder, call, timeout: float, verbose: bool,
               crwl_timeout: float = DEFAULT_CRWL_TIMEOUT,
               wayback_timeout: float = DEFAULT_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT,
               pdf_timeout: float = DEFAULT_PDF_TIMEOUT, want_full: bool = False,
               walk_budget: float = DEFAULT_WALK_BUDGET) -> dict:
    """A provider returns (content, where) or (content, where, meta); meta (e.g. truncated_by)
    is merged into the result.

    want_full (fetch): a reply flagged truncated_by (a provider cap) is held and the ladder
    walks on. The first complete reply at least FULLER_SLACK times as long as the longest held
    one wins; at the end the longest reply is returned (truncated if it was capped). A rung
    whose RUNG_CAP is no larger than the held copy is skipped, and no rung starts more than
    walk_budget seconds after the first capped copy. The copies that did not win are listed
    in the result's "held" (provider, chars, truncated)."""
    attempts = []
    held: list[dict] = []  # successful replies that did not end the walk
    walk_t0 = None  # when the first capped copy arrived

    def finish(res: dict) -> dict:
        others = [{"provider": r["provider"], "chars": len(r["content"]),
                   "truncated": bool(r.get("truncated_by"))} for r in held if r is not res]
        if others:
            res["held"] = others
        return res

    def log(msg: str) -> None:
        if verbose:
            print(f"web-get: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)

    for name, fn in ladder:
        capped = max((len(r["content"]) for r in held if r.get("truncated_by")), default=0)
        if want_full and capped and RUNG_CAP.get(name, math.inf) <= capped:
            err = f"skipped: its cap ({RUNG_CAP[name]} chars) cannot beat the held capped copy"
            attempts.append({"provider": name, "ok": False, "error": err, "ms": 0})
            log(f"try {name}: SKIP {err}")
            continue
        if want_full and walk_t0 is not None and time.monotonic() - walk_t0 >= walk_budget:
            err = f"skipped: walk budget ({walk_budget:g} s after the capped copy) spent"
            attempts.append({"provider": name, "ok": False, "error": err, "ms": 0})
            log(f"try {name}: SKIP {err}")
            continue
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        budget = provider_timeout(name, timeout, crwl_timeout, wayback_timeout, pdf_timeout)
        try:
            got = guarded(budget, lambda: call(fn, Deadline(budget)))
            content, where = got[0], got[1]
            meta = got[2] if len(got) > 2 else {}
            ms = int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)
            row = {"provider": name, "ok": True, "error": None, "ms": ms, "chars": len(content)}
            attempts.append(row)
            res = {"ok": True, "provider": name, "url": where, "content": content,
                   "attempts": attempts, **meta}
            if want_full and meta.get("truncated_by"):
                row["truncated"] = True
                held.append(res)
                if walk_t0 is None:
                    walk_t0 = time.monotonic()
                log(f"try {name}: TRUNCATED ({ms} ms, {len(content)} chars, cap "
                    f"{meta.get('truncated_to')}); walking on for a fuller copy")
                continue
            if want_full and capped and len(content) < FULLER_SLACK * capped:
                row["note"] = f"shorter than the held capped copy ({capped} chars)"
                held.append(res)
                log(f"try {name}: ok but SHORT ({ms} ms, {len(content)} chars < "
                    f"{FULLER_SLACK} x {capped}); walking on")
                continue
            log(f"try {name}: ok ({ms} ms, {len(content)} chars)")
            return finish(res)
        except ProviderError as e:
            err = redact(str(e))
        except _HardTimeout:
            err = "timeout (hard guard)"
        except Exception as e:  # a provider bug must not stop the ladder
            err = redact(f"internal error: {type(e).__name__}: {e}")
        ms = int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)
        attempts.append({"provider": name, "ok": False, "error": err, "ms": ms})
        log(f"try {name}: FAIL ({ms} ms) {err}")
    best = max(held, key=lambda r: len(r["content"]), default=None)
    if best:
        return finish(best)
    return {"ok": False, "provider": None, "url": None, "content": None, "attempts": attempts}


_PATH_SAFE = "/%:@!$&'()*+,;=-._~"
_QUERY_SAFE = _PATH_SAFE + "?"


def normalize_url(url: str) -> str:
    """IDNA-encode the host and percent-encode path, query and fragment (idempotent)."""
    p = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)
    host = p.hostname or ""
    try:
        host_a = host.encode("idna").decode("ascii") if host and not host.isascii() else host
    except UnicodeError:
        host_a = host
    if ":" in host_a:  # IPv6 literal
        host_a = f"[{host_a}]"
    netloc = host_a
    if p.port:
        netloc += f":{p.port}"
    if p.username is not None:
        cred = urllib.parse.quote(p.username, safe="%")
        if p.password is not None:
            cred += ":" + urllib.parse.quote(p.password, safe="%")
        netloc = f"{cred}@{netloc}"
    return urllib.parse.urlunsplit((
        p.scheme, netloc, urllib.parse.quote(p.path, safe=_PATH_SAFE),
        urllib.parse.quote(p.query, safe=_QUERY_SAFE), urllib.parse.quote(p.fragment, safe=_QUERY_SAFE)))


def truncate_bytes(text: str, n: int) -> str:
    if n <= 0:
        return text
    b = text.encode("utf-8")
    return text if len(b) <= n else b[:n].decode("utf-8", "ignore")


def emit(kind: str, target: str, res: dict, as_json: bool) -> int:
    res = {"ok": res["ok"], "kind": kind, "target": target, **res}
    if res["ok"]:
        where = res["url"] or target
        label = "query" if kind == "search" and not res["url"] else "url"
        print(f"web-get: provider={res['provider']} {label}={where}", file=sys.stderr)
        capped = res.get("truncated_by") in CAPPED_PROVIDERS
        if capped:
            print(f"web-get: truncated: {res['truncated_by']} returned its "
                  f"{res['truncated_to']}-character cap (maxCharacters) and no other rung "
                  "gave a fuller copy; the page is longer — not yet fetched (operator rule "
                  "2026-10-11, exit 6): try other URL forms, fix the tool, or pause",
                  file=sys.stderr)
        if res.get("max_bytes_cut"):
            print(f"web-get: truncated to {res['max_bytes_cut']} bytes (--max-bytes); the page "
                  "is longer", file=sys.stderr)
        if res.get("snapshot"):
            print("web-get: served from a Wayback Machine snapshot, not the live page",
                  file=sys.stderr)
        if as_json:
            print(json.dumps(res, ensure_ascii=False))
        else:
            sys.stdout.write(res["content"].rstrip("\n") + "\n")
        return EXIT_TRUNCATED if capped else EXIT_OK
    summary = "; ".join(f"{a['provider']}: {a['error']} ({a['ms']} ms)" for a in res["attempts"])
    print(f"web-get: {PAUSE_MSG}; {kind} {target!r}; attempts: {summary or 'none (all skipped)'}",
          file=sys.stderr)
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(res, ensure_ascii=False))
    return EXIT_ALL_FAILED


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- check


def cmd_check(only, skip, timeout, as_json, verbose, crwl_timeout=DEFAULT_CRWL_TIMEOUT,
              wayback_timeout=DEFAULT_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT, pdf_timeout=DEFAULT_PDF_TIMEOUT) -> int:
    """Narrowed by --only/--skip, ok means every selected probe is healthy; else the full
    threshold (>= 3 healthy, one search and one fetch among them)."""
    probe_url = env("WEB_GET_CHECK_URL", "https://example.com/")
    pdf_url = env("WEB_GET_CHECK_PDF_URL", "https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-pdf/fw9.pdf")
    jobs = []
    for name, fn in select(SEARCH, only, skip):
        jobs.append(("search", name, lambda fn=fn: fn("web-get health check", 1, Deadline(timeout))))
    for name, fn in select(FETCH, only, skip):
        t = provider_timeout(name, timeout, crwl_timeout, wayback_timeout, pdf_timeout)
        u = pdf_url if name == "pdf" else probe_url
        jobs.append(("fetch", name, lambda fn=fn, t=t, u=u: _probe_fetch(fn, u, t)))
    if not jobs:
        print("web-get: no providers selected", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    _resolve_keys()  # once, before threads start

    def run(job):
        kind, name, thunk = job
        t0 = time.monotonic()
        try:
            thunk()
            return kind, name, True, None, int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)
        except ProviderError as e:
            return kind, name, False, redact(str(e)), int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)
        except Exception as e:
            return kind, name, False, redact(f"internal error: {e}"), int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000)

    ex = concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=len(jobs))
    futs = [ex.submit(run, j) for j in jobs]
    longest = max(timeout, crwl_timeout, wayback_timeout, pdf_timeout)
    concurrent.futures.wait(futs, timeout=longest + GUARD_SLACK)
    rows, hung = [], False
    for j, fu in zip(jobs, futs):
        if fu.done():
            rows.append(fu.result())
        else:  # a probe outlived its deadline: report it, and do not wait for its thread
            hung = True
            rows.append((j[0], j[1], False, "timeout (hard guard)",
                         int(1000 * (longest + GUARD_SLACK))))
    ex.shutdown(wait=not hung, cancel_futures=True)
    healthy = [r for r in rows if r[2]]
    kinds = {r[0] for r in healthy}
    narrowed = bool(only or skip)
    ok = (len(healthy) == len(rows)) if narrowed else (
        len(healthy) >= 3 and {"search", "fetch"} <= kinds)
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps({"ok": ok, "healthy": len(healthy), "providers": [
            {"kind": k, "provider": n, "ok": g, "error": e, "ms": ms} for k, n, g, e, ms in rows]}))
    else:
        for k, n, g, e, ms in rows:
            print(f"{k:6} {n:12} {'ok  ' if g else 'FAIL'} {ms:6d} ms" + (f"  {e}" if e else ""))
        if not jina_key():
            print(f"note: no Jina key ({key_note('JINA_API_KEY')}); jina-mcp/jina-search unavailable, "
                  "jina-reader keyless", file=sys.stderr)
        if not exa_key():
            print(f"note: no Exa key ({key_note('EXA_API_KEY')}); exa-api unavailable, exa-mcp "
                  "keyless", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.stdout.flush()
    if ok:
        why = ""
    elif narrowed:
        why = " — not every selected provider is healthy"
    else:
        why = f" — need >= 3 incl. one search and one fetch; {PAUSE_MSG}"
    print(f"web-get check: {len(healthy)}/{len(rows)} healthy{why}", file=sys.stderr)
    rc = EXIT_OK if ok else EXIT_ALL_FAILED
    if hung:
        sys.stderr.flush()
        kill_children()
        cleanup_tmpdirs()
        os._exit(rc)
    return rc


def _probe_fetch(fn, url, timeout):
    """A probe only needs a real page back; example.com is shorter than MIN_FETCH_CHARS."""
    try:
        return fn(url, Deadline(timeout), 20000)
    except ProviderError as e:
        m = re.match(r"near-empty content \((\d+) chars\)", str(e))
        if m and int(m.group(1)) >= 50:
            return "", url
        raise


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- main


def rung_budget(flag: float | None, var: str, default: float, timeout: float) -> float:
    """A rung's own budget: the flag, else $var, else max(default, --timeout)."""
    if flag is not None:
        return flag
    raw = os.environ.get(var, "").strip()
    if raw:
        try:
            return float(raw)
        except ValueError:
            raise ValueError(f"${var}={raw!r} is not a number of seconds") from None
    return max(default, timeout) if math.isfinite(timeout) else default


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    common = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)
    common.add_argument("--only", help="comma list of providers to use (others skipped)")
    common.add_argument("--skip", help="comma list of providers to skip")
    common.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=DEFAULT_TIMEOUT,
                        help="wall-clock seconds per provider attempt (default 45)")
    common.add_argument("--crwl-timeout", type=float, default=None,
                        help="seconds for the crawl4ai attempt (default max(150, --timeout), "
                             "$WEB_GET_CRWL_TIMEOUT)")
    common.add_argument("--wayback-timeout", type=float, default=None,
                        help="seconds for the wayback attempt (default max(120, --timeout), "
                             "$WEB_GET_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT)")
    common.add_argument("--pdf-timeout", type=float, default=None,
                        help="seconds for the pdf attempt (default max(120, --timeout), "
                             "$WEB_GET_PDF_TIMEOUT)")
    common.add_argument("--walk-budget", type=float, default=None,
                        help="fetch: seconds the ladder may keep walking after a provider-capped "
                             "copy (default 300, $WEB_GET_WALK_BUDGET)")
    common.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="JSON object on stdout")
    common.add_argument("--verbose", "-v", action="store_true", help="log each attempt to stderr")
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="web-get", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0],
                                 epilog="Exit 0 ok, 2 usage, 5 all providers failed (PAUSE), "
                                        "6 fetch cut at a provider cap (not yet fetched).")
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    s = sub.add_parser("search", parents=[common], help="web search through the ladder")
    s.add_argument("query")
    s.add_argument("--n", type=int, default=8, help="number of results (default 8)")
    f = sub.add_parser("fetch", parents=[common], help="fetch one page through the ladder")
    f.add_argument("url")
    f.add_argument("--max-bytes", type=int, default=0, help="truncate content to N bytes")
    f.add_argument("--no-page-check", action="store_true",
                   help="accept a page the wrong-page heuristic would reject (checked by you)")
    sub.add_parser("check", parents=[common], help="probe every provider once")
    a = ap.parse_args(argv)

    try:
        only, skip = parse_set(a.only), parse_set(a.skip)
    except ValueError as e:
        print(f"web-get: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    try:
        a.crwl_timeout = rung_budget(a.crwl_timeout, "WEB_GET_CRWL_TIMEOUT",
                                     DEFAULT_CRWL_TIMEOUT, a.timeout)
        a.wayback_timeout = rung_budget(a.wayback_timeout, "WEB_GET_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT",
                                        DEFAULT_WAYBACK_TIMEOUT, a.timeout)
        a.pdf_timeout = rung_budget(a.pdf_timeout, "WEB_GET_PDF_TIMEOUT",
                                    DEFAULT_PDF_TIMEOUT, a.timeout)
        a.walk_budget = rung_budget(a.walk_budget, "WEB_GET_WALK_BUDGET",
                                    DEFAULT_WALK_BUDGET, -math.inf)
    except ValueError as e:
        print(f"web-get: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    if not all(math.isfinite(x) and x > 0 for x in (a.timeout, a.crwl_timeout, a.wayback_timeout,
                                                      a.pdf_timeout, a.walk_budget)):
        print("web-get: --timeout, --crwl-timeout, --wayback-timeout, --pdf-timeout and "
              "--walk-budget must be finite and > 0", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    install_signal_handlers()

    if a.cmd == "check":
        return cmd_check(only, skip, a.timeout, a.json, a.verbose, a.crwl_timeout,
                         a.wayback_timeout, a.pdf_timeout)

    if a.cmd == "search":
        q = a.query.strip()
        if not q or a.n < 1:
            print("web-get: empty query or --n < 1", file=sys.stderr)
            return EXIT_USAGE
        ladder = select(SEARCH, only, skip)
        if not ladder:
            print("web-get: no search providers left after --only/--skip", file=sys.stderr)
            return EXIT_USAGE
        if KEYED_RUNGS & {n for n, _ in ladder}:
            _resolve_keys()  # before the ladder: never inside a rung's budget or SIGALRM guard
        res = run_ladder(ladder, lambda fn, dl: fn(q, min(a.n, 25), dl), a.timeout, a.verbose,
                         a.crwl_timeout, a.wayback_timeout, a.pdf_timeout)
        return emit("search", q, res, a.json)

    url = a.url.strip()
    p = urllib.parse.urlsplit(url)
    if p.scheme not in ("http", "https") or not p.netloc:
        print(f"web-get: not an http(s) URL: {url!r}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    try:
        url = normalize_url(url)
    except ValueError as e:
        print(f"web-get: bad URL {a.url.strip()!r}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    ladder = select(FETCH, only, skip)
    if not ladder:
        print("web-get: no fetch providers left after --only/--skip", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE
    _page_check["on"] = not a.no_page_check
    if KEYED_RUNGS & {n for n, _ in ladder}:
        _resolve_keys()  # before the ladder: never inside a rung's budget or SIGALRM guard
    # Exa always gets its full cap, so a small --max-bytes cannot make its reply near-empty
    # and a reply at the cap reliably means Exa cut the page; a capped reply makes the ladder
    # walk on (want_full), a --max-bytes cut below is the caller's choice and never does.
    res = run_ladder(ladder, lambda fn, dl: fn(url, dl, EXA_MAX_CHARS), a.timeout, a.verbose,
                     a.crwl_timeout, a.wayback_timeout, a.pdf_timeout, want_full=True,
                     walk_budget=a.walk_budget)
    res["truncated"] = bool(res.get("truncated_by"))
    if res["ok"] and a.max_bytes > 0:
        cut = truncate_bytes(res["content"], a.max_bytes)
        if cut != res["content"]:
            res.update(content=cut, truncated=True, max_bytes_cut=a.max_bytes)
            if not res.get("truncated_by"):  # a provider cap stays the reason (exit 6)
                res.update(truncated_by="max-bytes", truncated_to=a.max_bytes)
    return emit("fetch", url, res, a.json)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main())
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        kill_children()
        sys.exit(130)
    except BrokenPipeError:
        sys.exit(0)
